CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --show-goto-functions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*std::optional<signed_int>::optional\(this,(ref|rref)_signed_int\).*$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
^.*invalid implicit conversion.*to 'struct optional'.*$
--
Regression for member-converting-constructor template deduction in
an instantiated namespaced class template (`std::optional<int>`).

`return x;` into a `std::optional<int>` return type copy-initializes
the optional from an `int` via its converting constructor
`optional(_Up&&)`.  The deduction needs the class template
parameter `_Tp` bound; that binding requires looking up the
enclosing class's tag-type symbol.

Without the fix, the tag-type name was reconstructed as
`tag-std::optional<int>` (tag- at the front) instead of the actual
`std::tag-optional<int>` (tag- after the namespace), so the lookup
failed, `_Tp` was unbound, the converting constructor's SFINAE
constraint `is_constructible<_Tp, _Up>` could not be evaluated, the
deduction was rejected, and the conversion failed with "invalid
implicit conversion from 'signed int' to 'struct optional'".

Verified at the goto-program level (full BMC of std::optional
exceeds symex memory limits): the goto program must contain the
converting-constructor call with the int rvalue, and must NOT
report the conversion error.

Four files in CBMC's own source — `substitute_symbols.cpp`,
`pointer_offset_size.cpp`, `source_location.cpp`, `c_types.cpp` —
return a value into a `std::optional` and hit this.
